  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Volunteers can give a closing reminder in rooms, and reception can display the remaining visiting time.\", \"decision\": \"How should a short closing reminder reach visitors?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nReception displays the remaining time before volunteers give room reminders. Visitors can notice the time before being approached.\nOne volunteer updates the time display while the others give room reminders. The shared and local messages change together.\nVolunteers give room reminders and then reception updates the shared time display. The visible message reinforces the spoken reminder."
    }
  ],
